  "id": "Compound::DB00126 - Gene::5351",
  "verbalization": "Vitamin C is shown to interact with Plod2 through binding, which is then linked to activities involving Plod1. The evidence suggests that Vitamin C influences Plod2, which in turn participates in processes that are associated with Plod1. These processes include the modification of lysine residues in collagens and peptides, which are critical for extracellular matrix formation. The shared participation of Plod1 in these activities implies a potential functional overlap between Plod2 and Plod1, possibly through shared enzymatic pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Vitamin C in modulating the activity of Plod1, potentially through its influence on Plod2. This relationship underscores the importance of considering the interplay between different enzymes in the context of metabolic and structural processes.",
